{"id": "EUVD-2026-97693", "enisaUuid": "f25de0c8-a99a-3438-99a7-7486886f853b", "description": "FreeRDP 3.0.0 before 3.32.0 contains a heap out-of-bounds read in freerdp_assistance_parse_all_elements_of() because it advances its parsing cursor without reducing the remaining length, letting the scan window exceed the decrypted ConnectionString2 buffer. Attackers can supply a crafted .msrcIncident invitation file and password that crash xfreerdp when opened, before any RDP connection.", "datePublished": "2026-10-12T16:04:22", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T16:56:51", "baseScore": 6.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/FreeRDP/FreeRDP/security/advisories/GHSA-gvq8-v2fm-ffxv", "https://github.com/FreeRDP/FreeRDP/commit/2a737ce14dfee036a12d2d3e87473ace3e20349b", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/freerdp-3.0.0-before-3.32.0-heap-out-of-bounds-read-via-remote-assistance-file-parsing"], "aliases": ["GHSA-jp53-9rp8-7w3q", "CVE-2026-109249"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.12, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "ca95a9c2-8625-36d0-9eea-1a58678c0b55", "product": {"name": "FreeRDP", "vendor": {"name": "FreeRDP"}}, "product_version": "3.0.0 <3.32.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "1afacf20-a976-3183-9640-81800ac29c8f", "vendor": {"name": "FreeRDP"}}], "isExploited": false}